  "interpretation": "On matched new Image, CONTROL and acknowledged-UPDATE rows stall. Controller SINGLE prepares one active request while retaining ten normal Ethernet buffers and completes the larger row. This is a guarded diagnostic workaround; mapping/preparation/overlap timing and exact hardware/DMA cause remain unresolved.",
  "limits": [
    "No sustained throughput/stability, other-port/board, suspend, persistent boot or ACM serial repair claim.",
    "No-response UPDATE Success is the software default without polling; acknowledged UPDATE status0 is a polled hardware return, not proof of data transfer progress.",
    "Prepared/giveback delta is justified by observed positive non512-multiple linear EEM requests with one normalTRB each; complete_trb events with HWO1 are not counted as successful retirement.",
    "Binary USBmon timestamps use CLOCK_REALTIME, sampled offset guard; target admission uses causal BOOTTIME. Raw payloads/URB pointers are never exported by the monitor.",
    "Unmodified original modules pass some smaller rows; this workload-specific differential does not establish serialization as necessary for every successful USB exchange."
  ]
}
